        "# Complex number\n",
        "\n",
        "A complex number has real and imaginary parts. Python writes the imaginary part with `j`, as in `3+4j`, and exposes the parts as `.real` and `.imag`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-complex-number)"
      ]
    }
